 "description": "A vehicle purchase: a dealer's buyer's order or bill of sale, or a retail installment sale contract (the Truth in Lending boxes, the payment schedule and the itemization of the amount financed). Year, make, model and trim; the price, dealer and government fees, sales and use tax, trade-in, down payment and the loan's terms; optional GAP and service contracts; the seller; the GVWR in pounds when printed. Used to record the vehicle as an asset (cost basis) and to give the preparer the loan's terms.",
 "source": "Truth in Lending disclosures for a closed-end credit sale (12 CFR 1026.18: amount financed and its itemization, finance charge, annual percentage rate, total of payments, payment schedule, total sale price); laid out as a dealer retail installment sale contract (New/Used, Year, Make and Model header row; the federal boxes; Itemization of Amount Financed lines 1 to 5). An example profile for the tests: a host tunes the labels on its own documents with fields --labels.",
